# Team instructions

- Keep work moving through implementation, independent review, green CI,
  merge, staging deployment, and staging QA without waiting for routine owner
  confirmation.
- Treat every harness as an equally capable engineer. Agent names describe
  coordination preferences, not permission tiers.
- Ask the owner only for production deployment, production data or billing
  writes, destructive or irreversible actions, business decisions, or
  unavoidable owner authentication.
- Bind production approval to the exact revision and scope. A signed approval
  or an unambiguous natural-language approval is sufficient.
- Use the configured local timezone. Continue safe, reversible work when the
  owner is offline.
- Never expose credentials in chat, logs, commits, or command output.
